-- title:
--   Radius loss through an entrance and its full reflection
-- statement:
--   In projective coordinates $y=(m,u,v,w)$ put
--   $k(y)=\sqrt{(m-1)^2+v^2}$. Write $Z(y)$ for the state at the
--   first positive unit entrance and $\kappa(y)=k(Z(y))$.
--   At the partial core's downward unit hit, let $p$ be
--   the three exit parameters, $G$ the reflected core state after its
--   connection, and $t_R$ the absolute arrival time on the original orbit.
--   Write $g=G_0$ and $X=2/g$. The physical endpoint identity says that
--   the ascending unit entry with core $G$ equals the reflection of the
--   projective state of this orbit at $t_R$.
--   Let $k(y)\ge8$, $m\ge1$, $0<u,w\le10^{-4}$,
--   $0<v<1$, $0<\eta\le10^{-4}$, $u+vw\le\eta/(2k(y))$. Then
--   $p_0,g\ge\kappa/2$, $1\le\kappa-g\le3$,
--   $|g-(\kappa-2)|\le64(Z_1+Z_3^2)/\kappa$ and
--   $0<G_1\le Z_1$, $0<G_2\le Z_3$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/l46430640-del/ERA-STATISTICS-FORMAL/blob/d74c241819f896ab8d050b21ace80c8e90eabd9e/BianchiIX/Dynamics/EntranceReflectionValues.lean#L10-L66

